WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.068
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.069
We're here with
Kimberly Williams-Paisley

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.270
and Ashley Williams.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.538
This is very cool.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.139
These are two separate movies.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:09.342
It might be confusing because we
can only show one clip.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.444
But you guys have been doing
this both for a long time.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.146
You've never acted in films
together before.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.480
-Never.
-And you got to do two movies

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.749
at the same time. How did this
come together as an idea?

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:18.417
-This is Ashley's idea.

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:19.986
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:22.121
I mean, it was.
-Okay.

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.923
-Yeah, I mean,
I've wanted to work with

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.791
my big sister my entire life.

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:28.695
I was her first fan before
all y'all came in here.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.796
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.364
So, you know, it was
a dream come true.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:34.300
And I came to her,
and, you know, I just --

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.970
This is my best friend,
my closest confidante,

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.105
the first phone call I make
when I'm crying

00:00:40.105 --> 00:00:41.173
or when I have good news.

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:44.077
And so I had this idea

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.512
that what if she was
the star of one movie

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:47.980
and I was the star
of another movie,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.985
and then our story lines sort of
wove back and forth throughout?

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.786
Which is kind of like a metaphor
for our lives.

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:56.622
Like, I'm this lead of the movie
of my life.

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:58.324
And she's the secondary
character.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.960
[ Laughter ]
And she's the lead of her movie

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.861
and I'm her best friend.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:02.861 --> 00:01:04.697
-So we just did that.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:08.067
And it was -- Hallmark was
so supportive of the idea.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.568
They were really,
really thrilled.

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:10.970
-We pitched it
like five years ago,

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.239
and it took a really long time
to figure out

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.674
how exactly they need to
weave together.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:15.975
-Sure.
-You know?

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.311
And just to get them going,
but we finally did it.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:21.380
And we produced, and Ashley's
husband Neal produced as well.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.615
-Mm-hmm.
-Brad wrote a song.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.451
-Brad wrote a great song
and Kelleigh Bannen sings.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.119
And it's just a beautiful --

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.488
Yeah, it's a beautiful part of
the movie.

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:31.190
-One of the things I've learned
about Hallmark movies

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.059
in recent years is that you --

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:35.261
they are shot in the middle of
the summer.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:38.030
-Yeah.
-And in, like -- This was Utah.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.532
-Yeah.
-Super hot.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.634
And we're, of course, like,
in winter coats, you know.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.836
-Right. This is actually --

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.204
So this is a real shot?

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.306
So you had a snowman and you had
to put an umbrella over it

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:50.142
'cause it would've melted.
-Our snowmen are such divas.

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:51.878
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:53.346
-It's like, "What about us?"

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.680
We're, like, sweating, but, no,
it's all about the snowmen.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.949
-No one's holding an umbrella
over our heads, yeah.

00:01:56.949 --> 00:02:01.387
So, yeah, because -- we had to
source the snow from local --

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.555
Where did we get our snow?

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.824
-Snow farms.
-I think a fish market. Yeah.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:09.262
So we -- And it was just blazing
sun, so we had to shield them.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.364
Yeah. Protect them.
-And how are your boys?

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:13.799
How many kids do you have?

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:15.501
-I have two. I have two boys.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.203
We only make boys.
-Okay, you make boys.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.538
-And we have a brother Jay
and he has three boys.

00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:22.075
So we have seven boys.
-Will your kids watch this?

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.043
Will they be excited to see
moms and aunts

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.244
in the same film together?

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:28.982
-Yeah, my 7-year-old watched --
The first movie,

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:32.185
"Sister Swap: Hometown Holiday,"
aired last night,

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:36.255
and my 7-year-old watched for
I think like 65 minutes

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:37.389
and then really politely said,

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:39.225
"I don't want to hurt
anyone's feelings,

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.528
but can I just do my own iPad?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:43.563
Which I thought was --
But I get it.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:46.065
He's 7, you know, he's 7.
-It's very nice that

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.067
he understood that
it might hurt feelings.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.470
-Yeah, well, he knows
his mother. I mean, yeah.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.804
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.473
-And my kids watched,
yeah, they watched last night.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.375
And I'm sure they'll watch yours
as well.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.876
-Well, it's fine.
-They're devoted fans.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.744
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:00.512
-Kim, that wasn't
super convincing.

00:03:00.512 --> 00:03:01.647
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:03.215
-And you know what?
I'm sure they will.

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:04.750
-I'm sure they would
try to watch.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.051
-They'll be very excited.

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:08.187
-I'm sure they would think about
watching yours. Yeah.

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:10.356
-We got to watch it together
last night, which was super fun.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.326
And we dropped in on a bunch of
Zooms and said hi to fans

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.261
who were watching,
and that was fun.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.095
-It's great.
It's really a lovely tradition,

00:03:17.095 --> 00:03:20.266
and people who care about
these films love them so much.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.334
And it's so cool to bring
something new to it.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.771
It's such a unique idea.
-Yeah, it's cool.

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.405
And last night we got to
watch the movie

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:29.708
with a very close family friend
named Anna Holbrook.

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:30.876
I'm not sure
if you guys are familiar,

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:33.145
but she was a soap star.

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:35.047
I first met her when I was 5.

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:36.349
-Yeah, I met her when I was 12.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.550
She took my first head shot.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.319
She was an actress, amazing,

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:41.754
and our mom's best friend --
-For 35 years.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.923
-And our mom passed away
five years ago,

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.825
so to have Anna Holbrook
playing our mom

00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:48.828
in these movies was,
like, unbelievable.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.063
And she's so great in it.
-She's amazing.

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:52.832
So we popped champagne
last night.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.033
-Yeah, we did.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.868
-Just delighted in
our own performances.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.970
[ Laughter ]
-We also have Kevin -- Yeah.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.538
We also have Kevin Nealon.
-Yep.

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:01.607
-Who I know is a friend of
all of ours as well

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:02.742
and his wife Susan Yeagley.
-Susan Yeagley was in it.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.309
-So we just, like, padded it

00:04:04.309 --> 00:04:06.144
with all of our friends
that we love so much.

00:04:06.144 --> 00:04:08.414
-Well, it's great, and it
definitely shows up on screen.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.048
And, you guys, it has just been
such a delight

00:04:10.048 --> 00:04:11.050
to have you both here.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.418
-It's so good to be here,
thank you.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.886
-Thank you so much.
You guys, give it up for

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:16.622
Kimberly Williams-Paisley
and Ashley Williams.

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:19.025
Check local listings
for reairing details.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.093
"Sister Swap:
Christmas in the City"

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.362
will premiere this Sunday
following the reairing of

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:24.897
"Sister Swap:
A Hometown Holiday"

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.566
as part of Hallmark Channel's
Countdown to Christmas.

